  "notes": "A Belgian tropical-house producer working from interpolations and remixes, named in the genre documentation as one of the key figures who established the style. The differentiating fact in his entry is what replaces the hat: \"a whistled or plucked hook substitutes for the hat's forward motion\", so the hat fill density is the lowest of the tropical block at 0.10, the open hat is near-absent, and the melody carries the whistle timbre and the forward motion instead — which is why its note density sits above the other tropical models here. The rest of the kit is \"soft four-square kick, clap on 2&4, offbeat shaker and light 16th percussion\". Harmony is \"major-mode four-chord loops with pentatonic melodic material, frequently inherited from an interpolated source\" `[LOW-CONF]`, a mark repeated here, and loops are 4 bars. The documented arrangement rule is the instrumental restatement of the hook after each chorus, so every structure places a bridge after a hook. Bass is \"rounded syncopated sub\". ⚠ The research says the parameters are sub-genre convention; that mark is repeated here, and every velocity, density and register above is INFERRED.",
